\subsection{A Clean 4-Step Monotonic Ladder on \texttt{v2.1}}
When evaluated on \texttt{v2.1}—the benchmark specifically designed to stress-test multi-task over-merging—our results form a crystal-clear, strictly monotonic progression (Figure~\ref{fig:pareto}B and Table~\ref{tab:main}):
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Step 1 — Unlocking Base SFT Without Any Training or Teacher Labels (Ideas C \& A):}
    Starting from \texttt{0\_sft2000} ($45.71\%$ Recall, $58.33\%$ Precision), multiplying just 4 \texttt{q\_norm} scalars by $1.35\times$ (\textbf{Idea C}) lifts Recall to $51.96\%$ ($+6.25\text{pp}$). Editing the top-64 newline/comma columns in L26--L31 \texttt{mlp.down\_proj} (\textbf{Idea A}: $2.0\times$ newline columns, $0.0\times$ comma columns) jumps \texttt{v2.1} Recall to \textbf{$57.93\%$ ($+12.22\text{pp}$)} and Precision to \textbf{$61.29\%$ ($+2.96\text{pp}$)}—closing \textbf{$90\%$} of the Recall gap to 150-step OPSD ($59.36\%$) in \textbf{zero training steps}!
    \item \textbf{Step 2 — Single-Model Late-Layer Denoising on Astra-SFT (Idea B-2):}
    Zeroing the top-2 singular values $\sigma_1 = \sigma_2 = 0$ in L18--L31 of \texttt{sft\_astra} (\textbf{Idea B-2}, touching only 2 scalars per module and no OPSD weights) improves \texttt{v2.1} Precision from $65.08\%$ to $66.13\%$ ($+1.05\text{pp}$) at $60.25\%$ Recall while simultaneously recovering $+3.44\text{pp}$ Recall on \texttt{v1}.
    \item \textbf{Step 3 — Strict Dominance Over Both OPSD and SFT via Layer-18 Circuit Grafting (\texttt{Graft-18}):}
    Combining \texttt{sft\_astra}'s high-gain middle clustering layers (L00--L17) with \texttt{opsd\_astra}'s uncontaminated readout layers (L18--L31) achieves \textbf{$64.52\%$ Recall and $69.84\%$ Precision on \texttt{v2.1}}—beating \texttt{opsd\_astra} in \textbf{both} Recall ($+5.16\text{pp}$) and Precision ($+0.75\text{pp}$), and beating \texttt{sft\_astra} by $+4.27\text{pp}$ Recall and $+4.76\text{pp}$ Precision.
    \item \textbf{Step 4 — Parameter-Free Spectral Consensus (\texttt{SVD-Blend-50/50}):}
    Computing the exact rank-16 SVD of $\frac{1}{2}\Delta W_{\text{OPSD}} + \frac{1}{2}\Delta W_{\text{SFT}}$ across all 32 layers without manual layer selection achieves \textbf{$72.41\%$ Initial Precision ($+3.32\text{pp}$ over OPSD, $+7.33\text{pp}$ over SFT)} and \textbf{$64.42\%$ Recall ($+5.06\text{pp}$ over OPSD)}.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Case-Level Evidence on \texttt{v2.1}}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{\texttt{JH02} (25 tabs: Soccer Balls, Grok AI, Manchester City, Exploratory Data Analysis):} Base \texttt{sft2000} dumps all 25 tabs into \texttt{Soccer: 1..25} ($0\%$ P, $0\%$ R). \textbf{Idea A} (zero training on \texttt{sft2000}) cleanly splits \texttt{Amazon: 1,6,17,23,25 | Grok: 2,3,4,11,13,14,20 | Manchester City: 5,8,9,10,12,16,19 | Data Analysis: 7,18,21,22} ($75.0\%$ P, $60.0\%$ R).
    \item \textbf{\texttt{JH16} (13 tabs: Minecraft, Khan Academy, Language Learning, Elyon Christian School):} Base \texttt{sft2000} scores $33.3\%$ Recall; \texttt{sft\_astra} loses \texttt{Elyon Christian School: 6, 9} into \texttt{Ungrouped} ($50.0\%$ R). \textbf{Idea A} achieves \textbf{$100.0\%$ P and $100.0\%$ R}, and both \textbf{Idea B-2} and \textbf{\texttt{Graft-18}} rescue \texttt{Elyon Christian School: 6, 9} ($75.0\%$ P, $75.0\%$ R).
    \item \textbf{\texttt{JH11} (33 tabs across 7 fine-grained sub-tasks):} \texttt{opsd\_astra} emits 4 broad groups (\texttt{Travel, AI, Slang, NBA}; $28.6\%$ R), whereas \textbf{\texttt{Graft-18}} and \textbf{Idea B-2} resolve all 7 fine-grained sub-tasks (\texttt{Travel Luggage, San Francisco Airbnb, Kimi AI Models, AI Decision Making, Copium Slang, NBA 2K26, NBA Players}; $85.7\%$ P, $85.7\%$ R).
\end{itemize}

\section{Conclusion}
Weight-space anatomy reveals a sharp functional division in post-trained LoRA adapters: middle layers (L08--L15) govern relational sub-task clustering, while late layers (L18--L31) control lexical formatting and readout thresholds. On complex multi-task tab grouping (\texttt{v2.1}), single-model neuron surgery (\textbf{Idea A}) recovers $+12.22\text{pp}$ Recall without training, and dual-adapter spectral surgery (\textbf{\texttt{Graft-18}} and \textbf{\texttt{SVD-Blend-50/50}}) strictly outperforms both OPSD and SFT across every metric.

