\subsection{How Diagnosis in Figure~\ref{fig:heatmap} Directly Dictates Every Surgical Intervention}
Computing the exact $32\times 32$ QR-SVD of $\Delta W_m = s(B_{1,m} A_{1,m} - B_{0,m} A_{0,m})$ relative to \texttt{sft2000} reveals three causal laws that directly guide our experiments:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Law 1 (Middle-Layer Clustering Resonance in L08--L15):} In Figure~\ref{fig:heatmap}(A), directional alignment between OPSD and Astra-SFT is highest in layers 8--15, specifically inside the attention matching modules \texttt{Attn InProj} ($\cos = 0.41$ at L10, $0.38$ at L12) and \texttt{Attn Gate/KV} ($\cos = 0.40$ at L10, $0.38$ at L12). Furthermore, because off-policy SFT applies unclipped cross-entropy across all tokens, its update magnitude in L08--L17 is $1.54\times$--$1.71\times$ larger than OPSD's lazy trajectory gradients (Figure~\ref{fig:heatmap}C). \emph{Implication:} To maximize sub-task splitting on \texttt{v2.1}, we should either sharpen middle-layer attention (\textbf{Idea C}) or harvest SFT's stronger L00--L17 representations (\textbf{\texttt{Graft-18}}).
    \item \textbf{Law 2 (Late-Layer Readout Contamination in L18--L31):} At Layer 18, $\cos(\Delta W_{\text{OPSD}}, \Delta W_{\text{SFT}})$ drops abruptly to $0.01$--$0.15$. Projecting the residual writers (\texttt{MLP DownProj} and \texttt{Attn OutProj}) onto the RMSNorm-weighted unembedding matrix $U_{\text{eff}}$ (Figure~\ref{fig:heatmap}B) shows that \texttt{sft\_astra}'s leading singular mode $u_1$ writes $8\times$--$11\times$ more strongly toward \texttt{' \&'} (reflecting the $9.1\times$ higher frequency of \texttt{' \& '} compound group names in Astra's labels) and shifts thresholds toward \texttt{Ungrouped}. \emph{Implication:} Excising the top singular scalars $\sigma_1, \sigma_2$ in L18--L31 (\textbf{Idea B}) or replacing L18--L31 with OPSD's clean readout (\textbf{\texttt{Graft-18}} / \textbf{\texttt{SVD-Blend}}) will eliminate late-layer noise while preserving fine-grained splitting.
    \item \textbf{Law 3 (Atomic Split-vs-Merge Valves in Late \texttt{MLP DownProj}):} Because \texttt{MLP DownProj} in L26--L31 directly writes into the final unembedding subspace, projecting its 9,216 columns onto $v_{\text{split}} = \hat{u}_{\texttt{\textbackslash n}} - \hat{u}_{\texttt{,}}$ isolates the exact neurons that trigger group termination versus giant-bucket continuation (\textbf{Idea A}, Figure~\ref{fig:pareto}A).
\end{itemize}

