25|\begin{abstract}
26|When adapting Small Language Models (SLMs) toward a frontier teacher on structured multi-entity generation tasks such as Browser Tab Grouping, practitioners face a sharp trade-off between off-policy Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT) and On-Policy Self-Distillation (OPSD). On \texttt{Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B} (32 layers, 21.2M LoRA parameters across 248 modules), training on 1,200 frontier (\texttt{GPT-6-astra}) reference solutions via off-policy SFT yields strong fine-grained sub-task splitting on complex sessions (\texttt{v2.1}), but causes a catastrophic \textbf{$-8.33\text{pp}$ to $-9.90\text{pp}$ Recall collapse} on standard sessions (\texttt{v1}). Conversely, OPSD preserves \texttt{v1} Recall ($72.52\%$ Run-1 / $70.20\%$ 3-run) while fixing giant-bucket over-merging, yet splits complex multi-task sessions less aggressively than SFT.
27|
28|Inspired by recent advances in \emph{Weight-Space Programming} (Takehi et al., 2026), we perform a full 32-layer QR-SVD and unembedding-projection anatomy of the effective LoRA weight updates $\Delta W = W - W_0$ without running gradients. We uncover an exact structural bifurcation at \textbf{Layer 18}: (1) middle layers (\textbf{L08--L15}) learn a shared cross-tab clustering circuit ($\cos(\Delta W_{\text{OPSD}}, \Delta W_{\text{SFT}}) \text{ up to } 0.37$), whereas (2) late layers (\textbf{L18--L31}) become nearly orthogonal ($\cos \text{ down to } 0.05$), where off-policy SFT's top singular directions project $8\times$--$11\times$ more strongly onto surface lexical artifacts (\texttt{' \&'}) and aggressive \texttt{Ungrouped} rejection thresholds. Armed with this white-box map, we demonstrate two families of \textbf{zero-training weight-space surgery}: (i) \emph{Single-Model Neuron/Scalar Edits} (Ideas A, B, C), where scaling just 64 newline-vs-comma MLP columns per layer in L26--L31 of the base SFT model lifts \texttt{v2.1} Recall from $45.71\%$ to $57.93\%$ ($+12.22\text{pp}$) with zero training and without touching OPSD; and (ii) \emph{Dual-Adapter Circuit Grafting \& Spectral Consensus} (\texttt{Graft-18} and \texttt{SVD-Blend-50/50}), which push \texttt{v2.1} Recall to \textbf{$64.52\%$} ($+5.16\text{pp}$ over OPSD) and Initial Precision to \textbf{$72.41\%$}, surpassing both parent paradigms.
