128|\begin{itemize}
129|    \item \textbf{\texttt{v2.1 / JH02} (25 tabs across Soccer Balls, Grok AI, Manchester City, Data Analysis):} Base \texttt{sft2000} collapses all 25 tabs into a single \texttt{Soccer: 1..25} bucket ($0\%$ Recall). \textbf{Idea A} (editing 64 columns in L26--L31 of \texttt{sft2000} with zero training) cleanly separates \texttt{Amazon: 1,6,17,23,25 | Grok: 2,3,4,11,13,14,20 | Manchester City: 5,8,9,10,12,16,19 | Data Analysis: 7,18,21,22} ($75.0\%$ P, $60.0\%$ R).
130|    \item \textbf{\texttt{v2.1 / JH16} (13 tabs):} Base \texttt{sft2000} merges non-Minecraft tabs into one coarse \texttt{Education} group ($33.3\%$ R), while \texttt{sft\_astra} drops \texttt{Elyon Christian School: 6, 9} into \texttt{Ungrouped}. \textbf{Idea A} achieves \textbf{$100.0\%$ Precision and $100.0\%$ Recall}, and both \textbf{Idea B-2} ($\sigma_1=\sigma_2=0$) and \textbf{\texttt{Graft-18}} rescue \texttt{Elyon Christian School: 6, 9} ($75.0\%$ R).
