134|\section{Conclusion}
135|Weight-space SVD and unembedding projections make LoRA post-training transparent: middle layers (L08--L15) encode cross-entity relational clustering, whereas late layers (L18--L31) govern lexical formatting and \texttt{Ungrouped} readout thresholds. Single-model neuron/scalar surgery (Ideas A, B, C) repairs over-merging and threshold overshoot in zero training steps, while dual-adapter spectral consensus (\texttt{SVD-Blend-50/50} and \texttt{Graft-18}) establishes a new Pareto frontier beyond both SFT and OPSD.
