66|Via reduced QR factorizations $Q_B R_B = s[B_{1,m}, -B_{0,m}]$ and $Q_A R_A = [A_{1,m}^\top, A_{0,m}^\top]$, the SVD of the full $d_{\text{out}} \times d_{\text{in}}$ matrix reduces exactly to a $32 \times 32$ core SVD $R_B R_A^\top = \tilde{U} \Sigma \tilde{V}^\top$, yielding exact left/right singular vectors $U = Q_B \tilde{U}$ and $V = Q_A \tilde{V}$. For residual-writing modules (\texttt{mlp.down\_proj}, \texttt{self\_attn.o\_proj}, \texttt{linear\_attn.out\_proj}) where $d_{\text{out}} = 2560$, we project $\Delta W_m$ and its leading left singular vector $u_1$ onto the RMSNorm-weighted unembedding matrix $U_{\text{eff}} = W_{\text{embed}} \odot \gamma_{\text{norm}} \in \mathbb{R}^{248320 \times 2560}$.
67|
